<%
# ==========================================================================
# MERIDIAN CYBER INSURANCE — ALBION COVERAGE DETERMINATION
# Case 3: Cyber Insurance (CyBOK Phase 7 SIS Project)
# Version: Draft 1 — April 2026
# ==========================================================================
#
# SCENARIO PREMISE
#   Thursday 7 May 2026, about seven weeks after the Albion incident (night of
#   Friday 20 to Saturday 21 March 2026, ESD pressed at about 06:34). The site
#   has been offline for six weeks and is back in service. Albion told Meridian
#   of the incident at 07:49 on 21 March and filed its £8.2M claim on Tuesday
#   5 May. Players are the Meridian Claims Team. Task: verify the forensic
#   causal chain, assess warranty compliance, and make a coverage recommendation.
#
#   Recommended predecessor: Case 2, "Albion Battery Hall: Code Red"
#   (scenarios/sis02_energy). Nothing carries over between the two games.
#
# ROOM LAYOUT
#   meridian_claims_suite (start) → north → meridian_evidence_archive (PIN locked)
#
# DEPLOYMENT
#   Copy to: BreakEscape/scenarios/sis03_cyber_insurance/scenario.json.erb
#   Ink files: scenarios/sis03_cyber_insurance/ink/
#   VM content: Hacktivity VM — meridian_forensic_review
#
# ==========================================================================
# IMPLEMENTATION STATUS
# ==========================================================================
#
# IMPLEMENTED — no additional work required
#   Pin locks (archive door, underwriting cabinet)
#   Readable note objects (all document props)
#   Phone NPC system (Whitworth, Hartley, Ngata) — full Ink dialogue trees compiled
#   Eleanor Vance person NPC — full Ink dialogue tree compiled
#   Forensic Data Platform terminal (MG-02) — self-contained client-side minigame,
#     no Hacktivity VM required
#   Claims Management System terminal (MG-01)
#   Warranty Compliance Checklist (MG-04)
#   Coverage Decision Form (MG-05)
#   eventMappings (all state transitions)
#
# PLACEHOLDER SPRITES — functional copies; replace with custom assets before release
#   coverage_decision_form.png  → copied from notes3.png
#   checklist.png               → copied from notes4.png
#   Eleanor Vance character     → using female_office_worker sprite (needs inspector_female variant)
#   meridian_claims_suite room  → using room_office tile set
#
# ==========================================================================
# ERB VARIABLES
# ==========================================================================

# Evidence Archive door PIN — printed on the access slip Eleanor hands over
# (itemsHeld, #give_item in npc_eleanor_vance.ink). Never put it in a voiced line
# or a bark: TTS caches by text, so a spoken PIN can't be randomised.
archive_pin = 6767 # @random_pin   
# Underwriting cabinet PIN — embedded in CMS policy notation
cabinet_pin = 5857 # @random_pin   
%>
{
  "scenario_brief": "Thursday 7 May 2026. You are the Meridian Cyber Insurance claims team. On Saturday 21 March a cyber attack on Albion Energy Storage, a grid battery site near Newark, switched off its safety trips and came close to a thermal runaway in Battery Hall 1. A hardwired emergency shutdown stopped it. The site was offline for six weeks and is now back in service. On Tuesday Albion filed an £8.2 million claim. Eleanor Vance, your Claims Manager, has opened the file; the forensic and loss adjustment reports are in. Your task: verify the causal chain, assess which policy warranties were breached, and make a coverage recommendation. The decision you reach will shape not just this claim, but the market's role in critical infrastructure security.",
  "show_scenario_brief": "on_resume",
  "disableAttacks": true,

  "startRoom": "meridian_claims_suite",

  "player": {
    "sprite": "male_nerd"
  },

