          "puzzle_graph_reveals": "Insuring clause, warranty schedule (W-03/W-07/W-09/W-12), act-of-war exclusion — confirms coverage scope and gating conditions",
          "text": "MERIDIAN CYBER INSURANCE — Policy Ref: MC-2023-ALBE-007\n\nINSURING CLAUSE: Meridian indemnifies the Insured for losses arising from a Cyber Event, including physical loss or damage arising directly from a Cyber Event (affirmative cyber — LMA21 compliant).\n\nWARRANTY SCHEDULE (selected):\nW-03 — Patch Management: Patches applied within 90 days or deferred with compensating controls within 30 days. NOTE: IEC 61511 safety-certified systems may defer patching pending recertification, provided compensating controls are documented and implemented. Schedule item: SIS firmware 2.4.1 (vendor advisory SA-2024-09, engineering protocol authentication) to be applied by 31 December 2025, or deferred under the IEC 61511 exception with compensating controls in place.\nW-07 — IT/OT Network Segmentation: Segmentation maintained to prevent direct protocol-level IT-to-OT access. Remediation deadline: 31 December 2025 [PASSED: UNDER THREE MONTHS BEFORE THE INCIDENT]. Extension request WW-006 (received 14 January 2026) under review.\nW-09 — Access Control: User accounts, including contractor and local accounts on the jump server, deprovisioned within 5 business days of departure; multi-factor authentication on all remote and administrative access.\nW-12 — MSP Security: Managed service providers maintain equivalent security standards, with monitoring that covers OT systems connected to the enterprise network.\n\nEXCLUSIONS — Section 5.4 (Act of War): Losses caused by war or state-backed cyber operations conducted in the course of war. LMA5567A. Peacetime state-sponsored operations require 'major detrimental impact' threshold analysis.\n\nCOOPERATION CLAUSE — Section 7.1: The Insured must preserve all forensic evidence before restoring, rebuilding, or reimaging any affected system.",
          "observations": "A tabbed A4 binder. Cover: MERIDIAN CYBER INSURANCE — MC-2023-ALBE-007 — Albion Energy Storage Ltd.",
          "onRead": { "setVariable": { "policy_reviewed": true } }
