          "puzzle_graph_role": "clue",
          "puzzle_graph_aim": "investigate_claim",
          "puzzle_graph_reveals": "£8.2M claim quantum breakdown; incident timeline; containment actions — contributes to investigate_claim aim",
          "text": "INCIDENT NOTIFICATION AND CLAIM: Meridian Claims Portal\nPolicy: MC-2023-ALBE-007\nFiled by: James Whitworth, General Manager, Albion Energy Storage Ltd\n\nPART 1: INITIAL NOTIFICATION, Saturday 21 March 2026, 07:49\nNotified by phone about 75 minutes after the emergency shutdown (within the 48-hour notification requirement); written notice the same day. Mr Whitworth was on annual leave and was briefed by phone by the site team.\nIncident type: confirmed cyber intrusion into SCADA/ICS systems\nSystems affected: PLC-BMS, SIS safety PLC, enterprise IT network\nPhysical: Battery Racks A1-A4 (Hall 1) overheated; cells did not reach thermal runaway\nContainment: hardwired ESD pressed about 06:34; jump server's network cable pulled 06:41; enterprise connections to the site isolated\nRegulatory: initial NIS notification sent 07:00 to Ofgem (acting jointly with DESNZ); NCSC told; NESO told of the frequency deviation\n\nPART 2: CLAIM, Tuesday 5 May 2026\nESTIMATED TOTAL LOSS: £8,200,000 (provisional)\n  Incident response and forensics: £1,100,000\n  Business interruption (whole site, 100 MW, offline 21 March to 2 May; lost frequency response and trading revenue, NESO non-delivery charges): £900,000\n  Physical damage (replacement battery modules, Racks A1-A4, Hall 1): £5,000,000\n  Revalidation and recommissioning (SIS revalidation including firmware 2.4.1, Hall 1 recommissioning, grid compliance retests): £800,000\n  Third-party liability, Trent Water Services (clean-up and investigation costs claimed from Albion): £400,000\n\nNote: Facility offline 6 weeks for forensic investigation, network remediation and SIS recertification (including the deferred firmware update). Returned to service 2 May 2026.",
          "observations": "James Whitworth's incident notification and claim: the first notice from the morning of the incident, and the claim Albion's general manager filed through the Meridian Claims Portal on Tuesday.",
